    },
    "message": "Run the rules of an EffectProgram's events in Rust and own effect_program_v1\n\nnative/src/rules/effects.rs has the guard, the five handlers of events/effects.py, the two reads of\nmodifier stacks and validate_effect_program_state, in tick and history forms. The handlers keep the\ncopy, check and swap of their Python rules, by the design for step 3. The pydantic contracts and\nthe rules of other modules are called by name. Anything but a success says Unsupported with the\nworld as it was, so the Python rule words the outcome.\n\nnative/src/state/effect_program.rs is the row. schedule_effect_program stays Python and reaches it\nthrough forwarded writes. benchmarks/rule_shadow/shadow_effects.py compares whole worlds per event.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
